ed on the fact that there was indeed a well attested medieval legend equating Xanten with Troy. The inherited local pronunciation is Santen /ˈsan.tən/, but it has now been widely displaced by the spelling pronunciation. Xanten is the only German locality in X- (though there are a few Bavarian ones, such as Gsellmühle, which are pronounced with initial /ks/)."]],"senses":[[37296,"xanten","name","Xanten (a town in Lower Rhine, North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany)",0]]},"anmaßet":{"inflections":[["anmaßet","anmaßen","plural,second-person,subjunctive,subjunctive-i,subordinate-clause"]]},"auszubrennen":{"inflections":[["auszubrennen","ausbrennen","infinitive,infinitive-zu"]]},"fortspüle":{"inflections":[["fortspüle","fortspülen","first-person,indicative,present,singular,subordinate-clause"]]},"hohltauben":{"inflections":[["hohltauben","hohltaube","plural"]]},"siebzigstes":{"inflections":[["siebzigstes","siebzigste","neuter,nominative,singular,strong,without-article"]]},"silberfuchses":{"inflections":[["silberfuchses","silberfuchs","genitive"]]}}}